cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss Rev-RoConformer, please cite this preprint project and the foundational works listed in the manuscript."
title: "Rev-RoConformer: Memory-Efficient Depth Scaling of Rotary Conformers for Automatic Speech Recognition"
type: article
authors:
  - name: "Base27-CVNSS Research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Base27-CVNSS/Rev-RoConformer"
url: "https://github.com/Base27-CVNSS/Rev-RoConformer"
version: "0.1.0-preprint"
date-released: 2026-07-25
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - automatic speech recognition
  - ASR
  - speech-to-text
  - Conformer
  - rotary position embedding
  - RoPE
  - reversible neural networks
  - memory-efficient training
  - deep learning
abstract: >-
  Rev-RoConformer is a research proposal for an automatic speech recognition
  encoder that combines RoPE-based global self-attention, Conformer-style
  local acoustic convolution, and RevNet/Reformer-style additive-coupling
  reversible blocks. The project focuses on depth-dependent activation-memory
  scaling and explicitly separates that problem from the quadratic sequence
  complexity of full self-attention. Empirical WER, throughput, and GPU-memory
  claims remain to be established by the published benchmark protocol.
